      "id": "19417",
      "key": "SFCC-856",
      "summary": "CSP hardening: nonce/hash-based script-src and style-src (csp-xss)",
      "description": "Context\nSurfaced by the SIT Gate's Lighthouse CI job (\nlighthouserc.js\n, \nlighthouse:recommended\n preset — in scope per this epic's \"CI/CD pipeline including... Lighthouse CI >90\"), running for the first time against a real deployed build (SIT bootstrap, 2026-09-01).\nThe \ncontent-security-policy\n header \nis\n present and correctly built (\noverrides/app/ssr/contentSecurityPolicy.ts\n, wired via \nhelmet()\n in \noverrides/app/ssr.js\n) — this is not a \"CSP missing\" bug. Lighthouse's \ncsp-xss\n audit is failing because the policy currently relies on broad allowances rather than nonces/hashes:\nstyle-src\n includes \n'unsafe-inline'\n — per the file's own comment, required by Chakra UI's runtime style injection (\nuseDefaults: true\n replaces rather than merges a directive when given explicitly, so \n'self'\n/\n'unsafe-inline'\n are spelled out there deliberately)\nscript-src\n includes \n'unsafe-eval'\n (via MRT's own additions, not this file) plus a number of third-party wildcard origins (Stripe, PayPal, Adyen, Measmerize, Google Pay/Maps)\nWhy this isn't a quick fix\nRemoving \n'unsafe-inline'\n without a nonce-based alternative would very likely break Chakra's styling across the whole app. Removing \n'unsafe-eval'\n risks breaking the already-integrated third-party payment/widget scripts. A real fix means:\nGenerating a per-request nonce and threading it through SSR rendering (Chakra's \n<CacheProvider>\n/emotion nonce support) and every inline \n<script>\nThis touches \noverrides/app/ssr.js\n, which is on the \nabsolute never-touch list\n in \nAGENTS.md\n/\nfrozenFiles.md\n — no Tier-1-approver exception applies to that file. Any change there needs the Integration/SI Partner owner directly, not just Claude-assisted review\nVerifying every third-party integration (payments, Measmerize, Google Maps/Pay) still functions under a tightened policy\nScope\nDesign a nonce (or hash-based) CSP strategy compatible with Chakra UI's emotion-based styling\nThread the nonce through SSR rendering — requires the \nssr.js\n owner (Integration/SI Partner)\nRe-verify third-party script/style integrations under the tightened policy\nConfirm \ncsp-xss\n passes in \nlighthouserc.js\n's \nlighthouse:recommended\n preset on the SIT Gate\nOut of scope\n (separate Lighthouse findings, not part of this story)\ninstallable-manifest\n, \nservice-worker\n, \nmaskable-icon\n, \nsplash-screen\n — see SFCC-855\nunused-javascript\n, \nvalid-source-maps\n, \nuses-rel-preconnect\n — bundle/build hygiene\nStatus:\n logged as a known, accepted SIT Gate failure for now rather than fixed same-day — decided 2026-09-01 given the ssr.js constraint and the risk of breaking styling/payments without dedicated testing.",
