    {
      "id": "19416",
      "key": "SFCC-855",
      "summary": "PWA installability: web app manifest, service worker, maskable icon, splash screen",
      "description": "Context\nSurfaced by the SIT Gate's Lighthouse CI job (\nlighthouserc.js\n, \nlighthouse:recommended\n preset — in scope per this epic's \"CI/CD pipeline including... Lighthouse CI >90\"), running for the first time against a real deployed build (SIT bootstrap, 2026-09-01). The full preset is being kept as-is rather than narrowed, so these failing audits stay visible on every release branch's SIT Gate until built.\nFailing audits (PWA installability group)\ninstallable-manifest\n — no web app manifest configured for install prompts\nservice-worker\n — no service worker registered (site isn't installable/offline-capable)\nmaskable-icon\n — manifest icons aren't maskable-safe for adaptive icon platforms\nsplash-screen\n — no splash screen configured for standalone/installed launch\nScope\nAdd a web app manifest (\nmanifest.json\n) with correct icons (including a maskable variant), theme colours, and start URL\nRegister a service worker (\nworker/main.js\n already exists as a Tier 1 file per \nfrozenFiles.md\n — coordinate with Integration/SI Partner owner rather than editing directly)\nConfirm splash-screen generation from the manifest config\nOut of scope\n (separate Lighthouse findings, not part of this story)\ncsp-xss\n — CSP hardening (unsafe-inline/unsafe-eval removal) is a separate, more involved security investigation\nunused-javascript\n, \nvalid-source-maps\n, \nuses-rel-preconnect\n — bundle/build hygiene, not installability\nAcceptance criteria\ninstallable-manifest\n, \nservice-worker\n, \nmaskable-icon\n, and \nsplash-screen\n all pass in \nlighthouserc.js\n's \nlighthouse:recommended\n preset on the SIT Gate",
