    {
      "id": "19167",
      "key": "SFCC-728",
      "summary": "Add Prod config pull — gated draft-PR workflow for undocumented live config",
      "description": "Context\nFollow-up to SFCC-727 (Tier A drift-check tool). Production sits entirely outside GitHub\nActions today (per \n.github/ENVIRONMENT_SETUP.md\n) and is promoted Stage → Prod via BM\nreplication, one-way. This story adds a controlled way to pull config \ndown\n from Prod so\nconfig that only ever got set live there can be surfaced and folded back into source\ncontrol — closing the loop described in \ndocs/config-drift-detection-plan.md\n's \"Prod\nconfig pull\" section.\nReuses SFCC-727's diff engine and orchestrator (\nconfig-drift-check.js --env=prod\n) — this\nstory is about the gating and the draft-PR generation, not a new diff mechanism.\nAcceptance Criteria\nAC1 — Protected Environment.\n A \nproduction\n GitHub Environment exists (or is\n  configured) with required reviewers, holding Prod OAuth credentials inaccessible to any\n  other job.\nAC2 — Manual trigger only.\n The Prod pull runs via \nworkflow_dispatch\n only — never on\n  a schedule/cron, unlike the dev/staging/UAT checks in SFCC-727.\nAC3 — Reuses existing pipeline.\n Running it triggers the same export → download → diff\n  pipeline as SFCC-727's orchestrator, scoped to Prod (\n--env=prod\n) — no duplicated\n  diff/orchestration logic.\nAC4 — realDrift reporting unchanged.\n \nrealDrift\n findings against Prod are reported\n  the same way as other environments (step summary + \nconfig-drift\n GitHub issue) — a human\n  decides which side is correct; nothing is auto-applied.\nAC5 — undocumentedLive produces a draft PR.\n \nundocumentedLive\n findings against Prod\n  open a \ndraft\n PR (not ready-for-review) proposing the addition to the relevant\n  \ndata/core\n/\ndata/vendor\n file(s), with a description of what was found and where it came\n  from.\nAC6 — No auto-commits.\n The workflow never commits directly to any branch — all\n  Prod-sourced changes land only via the draft PR for human review and merge.\nAC7 — Archive cleanup.\n The exported Prod archive is deleted from WebDAV after download,\n  same as SFCC-727 AC4.\nTest Scenarios (manual)\n#\nScenario\nSteps\nExpected Result\n1\nReviewer gate enforced\nTrigger the workflow without required-reviewer approval\nRun is blocked/pending until an approver approves it\n2\nIn-sync Prod\nApproved trigger against Prod, config matches source control\nZero findings; no PR opened\n3\nUndocumented live config\nApproved trigger where Prod has a non-secret preference not in source control\nA draft PR is opened with the correct file/diff; PR is in draft state, not auto-merge-ready\n4\nReal drift against Prod\nApproved trigger where Prod disagrees with source control on an existing value\nReported same as other environments (step summary + issue); no PR opened for this case\n5\nCredential isolation\nInspect other (non-\nproduction\n-Environment) workflow jobs\nProd OAuth credentials are not readable/accessible outside the gated job\n6\nArchive cleanup\nAfter a run, check \nimpex/src/instance/\n on Prod via \nb2c webdav ls\nExported archive has been deleted — nothing left behind\nDependencies:\n SFCC-727 (Tier A drift-check tool must exist first).\nReference:\n \ndocs/config-drift-detection-plan.md\n, \"Prod config pull\" section.",
      "status": {
        "name": "To Do",
