      "key": "SFCC-820",
      "summary": "search/section-header-container",
      "description": "As a Developer, I want a reusable \nsearch/section-header-container\n React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, so that it can render a section header above search results in \nsearch-open\n, supporting both a simple heading and a sub-navigation menu layout.\nThe component renders a section header that varies based on the \ntype\n prop of its \nsearch/header\n child. When type=Heading, it displays a simple heading. When type=Sub-Navigation Menu, it renders a horizontal navigation bar with toggleable labels and overflow controls. It does not own navigation logic or label content — these are passed as props from the parent.\nProps in scope:\nProp\nValues\nNotes\nsize (container)\nDesktop, Mobile, Tablet\nControls layout breakpoint of the container\ntype\nHeading, Sub-Navigation Menu\nControls which header variant is rendered\nsize (header)\nDesktop, Mobile\nControls layout breakpoint of the search/header child\nshowHeader\ntrue, false\nToggles the heading element; applies to both types\nshowSubNavigation\ntrue, false\nToggles the entire label row; Sub-Navigation Menu only\nshowLabel3\ntrue, false\nToggles third nav label when sub-navigation is visible; Sub-Navigation Menu only\nshowLabel4\ntrue, false\nToggles fourth nav label when sub-navigation is visible; Sub-Navigation Menu only\nshowLabel5\ntrue, false\nToggles fifth nav label when sub-navigation is visible; Sub-Navigation Menu only\nshowOverflowRight\ntrue, false\nToggles right overflow indicator; Sub-Navigation Menu only\nshowOverflowLeft\ntrue, false\nToggles left overflow indicator; Sub-Navigation Menu only",
