      "id": "18363",
      "key": "SFCC-197",
      "summary": "Product Image Management",
      "description": "As a\n Merchandiser,\nI want\n to merchandize the product images within SFCC,\nso that\n the storefront can reliably display optimised product imagery.\nProduct images are synced into SFCC through the MuleSoft Product feed. Video covered in separate user story — see \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-188\n and \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-302\n . \n\n\n\n\nWe need to categorize images in BM so that they can correctly render in the right pages:\nImage View Type\nM2 Name (for reference)\nDescription\nFlat Item Image\nBase\nItem/flat lay view — background less (PNG), required due to dynamic background colour. Primary on PLP, secondary on PDP. \n\n\nThis one is also used as the colour swatch selector image on PDP. Please note - not always primary on PDP - for example, on accessories this might be different.\nDetail Image\nColour Swatch Images\nClose up shot - will be used in the colour swatch selector on the expanded image gallery on PDP.\nModel Image\nModel Image\nModel view (hero image) and a way to tag a video or image as relevant to show on hover - e.g. it will show on a product card’s hover state on PLP. Often primary on PDP, not always\nHidden\nHidden\nWay to tag an image as hidden - this means you see the image on roll over (like on PLP, maybe home page) but once you click into the PDP then the image gallery no longer shows that one. Used today sometimes for runway styles.\nProduct Styling Image\nProduct Styling Image\nThis image will be used for the Shop the look picture.\nFront View\nN/A\nThis view type does not drive a specific place for the image to appear on the website but can help accommodate better alt text on product images\nSide View\nN/A\nThis view type does not drive a specific place for the image to appear on the website but can help accommodate better alt text on product images\nBack View\nN/A\nThis view type does not drive a specific place for the image to appear on the website but can help accommodate better alt text on product images\nExtra information:\nWe need to have one canonical view type folder in SFCC that gathers the entire image gallery and determines the order of the image gallery on PDP (suggested is View Type = Large). The display order should be adjustable.\nManual swatches for accessories - content team has to upload swatch images for these.\nRunway / Campaign imagery are also there - they come at the end of the carousel.\nWe can use the image view type to prepopulate the alt text - so combination of view type + product name (SFCC-31 )\nMaintaining documentation here on Confluence so we can discuss with the MuleSoft team later: \n04.4.5 Product Images — View Types & MuleSoft Mapping Rules - Adobe SFCC - Confluence",
